 "what": "Every table read out of the plugins of the load order, in the order they read each other. scripts/mods/Rebuild-ContentTables.ps1 runs them after a change to one of Thornswood's own plugins (game/content). tests/test-2923-own-plugins.js holds the list to the builders: every builder that reads a load order is a step here or is in notInChain with its reason, and no step reads a table a later step writes.",
 "fields": "tool is the builder. data and plugins are the names it takes the game's Data folder and the plugin list by (null: it takes none). reads are the tables it reads that a builder writes; readsBack is one it reads and a later step writes back; when that step changes it (Write-CutItems.js sorting a new plugin's recipes, #4087), Rebuild-ContentTables.ps1 runs the chain again from the reader, once. writes are what it writes. uses are the other files of the repository it reads that no builder writes, outside scripts, game/content, game/data and records (#3425: Build-SpellTable.ps1 reads the K panel's book in game/ui, which was named nowhere, so scripts/mods/Run-OnBox.ps1 never sent it and the box run stopped there); tests/test-2923-own-plugins.js reads each builder for such a file and holds this list to it. writesOffChain are what its builder writes only when it is run by hand with an option the chain does not give it (Build-NpcPopulation.py --write-runtime, #3120): they are written LF like a step's writes, and are not sent to the box or brought back.",
