 "notInChain": {
  "scripts/dev/Build-ResourceLocations.py": "Reads the server's load order from a server-settings file, like Build-NpcPopulation.py does when the collection's load order moves, and refuses any plugin whose bytes are not the ones npc-population.json pins, its Thornswood-Content.esp row included. So it is rebuilt from that settings file together with the catalogue when the collection's load order moves. The chain's own catalogue step (after Build-LastPlugin.py, #3120) keeps those pins on the repository's plugins.",
  "scripts/dev/Build-StationSites.py":"Comes before the content plugin, not after it: it measures where the plugin's stations stand, and scripts/mods/Add-ContentRecords.py writes them into the plugin from its table. docs/systems/station-placement.md says how a site changes.",
  "scripts/dev/Audit-PapyrusEvents.py": "An audit: it says which scripts in the load order register for which events and writes no table a server or another builder reads.",
  "scripts/mods/Audit-ModMenus.js": "An audit: it says where each mod settings menu keeps its values and writes no table a server or another builder reads.",
  "scripts/mods/Audit-Mods.ps1": "An audit of the game folder's own install (its archives, folders and plugin list), which is what it is about. It reads no plugin's records."
 }
